at source - Moderate fish and poultry - Limited red meat - Associated with reduced heart disease, diabetes, and cancer risk ### DASH Diet - Designed to lower blood pressure - High in fruits, vegetables, whole grains - Low in sodium, red meat, added sugars - Rich in potassium, calcium, magnesium ## Dietary Tips for Specific Conditions ### For Diabetes - Monitor carbohydrate intake - Choose low glycemic index foods - Eat regular meals to maintain blood sugar - Include fiber-rich foods - Limit refined sugars and processed foods ### For Heart Health - Reduce sodium to less than 2,300 mg/day - Increase omega-3 fatty acids - Limit saturated and trans fats - Eat plenty of fruits and vegetables - Choose whole grains over refined grains ### For Weight Management - Control portion sizes - Eat", ''relevance_score'': 0.6685968094245268}, {''title'': ''heart_disease'', ''content'': "Or 75 minutes of vigorous aerobic activity per week - Muscle-strengthening activities 2+ days per week ### Lifestyle - Don''t smoke or quit smoking - Maintain healthy weight (BMI 18.5-24.9) - Manage stress - Get adequate sleep (7-9 hours) - Limit alcohol consumption - Manage diabetes, high blood pressure, and cholesterol ## Treatment ### Medications - Statins (lower cholesterol) - ACE inhibitors or ARBs (lower blood pressure) - Beta-blockers (reduce heart workload) - Antiplatelet agents (prevent blood clots) - Diuretics (reduce fluid buildup) - Blood thinners (prevent clots) ### Surgical Procedures - Angioplasty and stent placement - Coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG) - Heart valve repair or replacement - Heart transplant (in severe cases) ## When to Seek Emergency Care Call emergency services immediately if you experience: - Chest pain lasting more than a few minutes - Severe shortness of breath - Fainting or loss of consciousness - Rapid or irregular heartbeat with dizziness - Sudden severe weakness or numbness - Sudden difficulty speaking", ''relevance_score'': 0.6608199219738776}]','2026-07-2