INSERT INTO messages VALUES(43,11,'user','i have headache and vomiting repeadtely what will be the problem','','2026-07-29 07:00:54.035511');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(44,11,'assistant',unistr('I am an AI assistant for informational support only. Not a substitute for professional medical advice. Always consult a healthcare professional.\u000a\u000aHeadaches accompanied by repeated vomiting can be caused by several conditions, some of which may require urgent medical attention. Here are some possible causes:\u000a\u000a### **Possible Causes:**\u000a1. **Migraine**\u000a   - Severe, throbbing headache (often on one side of the head)\u000a   - Nausea and vomiting\u000a   - Sensitivity to light, sound, or smells\u000a   - May last for hours to days\u000a\u000a2. **Viral or Bacterial Infection (e.g., Flu, Gastroenteritis, Meningitis)**\u000a   - Fever, body aches, fatigue (flu)\u000a   - Stomach pain, diarrhea (gastroenteritis)\u000a   - **Meningitis (medical emergency)** – Severe headache, stiff neck, high fever, confusion, rash (in some cases)\u000a\u000a3. **Food Poisoning or Stomach Virus**\u000a   - Nausea, vomiting, diarrhea\u000a   - Stomach cramps\u000a   - Possible fever\u000a\u000a4. **Dehydration**\u000a   - Dry mouth, dizziness, dark urine\u000a   - May occur due to excessive vomiting or diarrhea\u000a\u000a5. **Increased Intracranial Pressure (Medical Emergency)**\u000a   - Severe headache (worse in the morning or when lying down)\u000a   - Vomiting (often projectile)\u000a   - Blurred vision, confusion, or seizures\u000a   - Possible causes: Brain tumor, hemorrhage, or severe head injury\u000a\u000a6. **Heat Exhaustion or Heat Stroke**\u000a   - Headache, dizziness, nausea, vomiting\u000a   - Hot, dry skin (in heat stroke)\u000a   - Rapid pulse, confusion\u000a\u000a7. **Carbon Monoxide Poisoning (Medical Emergency)**\u000a   - Headache, dizziness, nausea, vomiting\u000a   - Confusion, weakness\u000a   - Often occurs in poorly ventilated spaces with gas heaters or car exhaust\u000a\u000a8. **Medication Side Effects or Overdose**\u000a   - Some medications (e.g., painkillers, antibiotics) can cause headaches and nausea\u000a\u000a### **When to Seek Emergency Medical Help Immediately:**\u000a- **Severe headache** (worst of your life)\u000a- **Stiff neck** (possible meningitis)\u000a- **Confusion, slurred speech, or seizures**\u000a- **Blurred or double vision**\u000a- **Weakness on one side of the body**\u000a- **Vomiting that won’t stop (risk of dehydration)**\u000a- **High fever (over 103°F / 39.4°C) with headache**\u000a- **Recent head injury**\u000a\u000a### **What You Can Do Now:**\u000a- **Stay hydrated** (sip water, oral rehydration solutions if available)\u000a- **Rest in a quiet, dark room** (if migraine is suspected)\u000a- **Avoid bright lights and loud noises**\u000a- **Take over-the-counter pain relief** (e.g., acetaminophen or ibuprofen, if no contraindications)\u000a- **Monitor symptoms closely** – if they worsen, seek medical help immediately\u000a\u000aSince your symptoms could indicate a serious condition, **I strongly recommend consulting a doctor or visiting an emergency room for proper evaluation and treatment.** If you experience any of the emergency warning signs listed above, **call emergency services (911 or local equivalent) right away.**'),'[{''title'': ''first_aid_basics'', ''content'': ''## Allergic Reactions (Anaphylaxis) ### Symptoms - Swelling of face, lips, throat - Difficulty breathing - Hives or rash - Rapid pulse - Dizziness or fainting - Nausea or vomiting ### Treatment 1. Use epinephrine auto-injector (EpiPen) if available 2. Call 911 immediately 3. Lay the person down, elevate legs 4. Give second dose after 5-15 minutes if no improvement 5. Monitor breathing and pulse ## Heat-Related Illnesses ### Heat Exhaustion - Heavy sweating, weakness, cold/pale/clammy skin - Move to cool place, loosen clothing, apply cool cloths - Sip water slowly - Seek medical attention if vomiting occurs ### Heat Stroke (Medical Emergency) - High body temperature (103°F or higher), hot/red/dry skin - Rapid pulse, confusion, unconsciousness - Call 911 immediately - Move to cooler environment - Cool body rapidly with cold water or ice packs - Do NOT give fluids if unconscious ## When NOT to Move Someone - Suspected spinal injury - Head, neck, or back pain - Arm or leg numbness - Fractures - Loss of consciousness without airway problems'', ''relevance_score'': 0.7444421039793007}, {''title'': ''Medical-report-1-2048'', ''content'': ''a MEDICAL REPORT = (2 8 cigs NAME: NATIONALITY: | SEX: | AGE: MARITAL STATUS: PASSPORT NO: | ISSUE PLACE: | ISSUE DATE: POSITION APPLIED FOR: PHOTO DEAR SIR/ MADAM PLEASE, ARRANGE TO EXAMINE THE ABOVE MENTIONED CANDIDATE AS TO HIS/HER FITNESS FOR THE ABOVE MENTIONED POSITION. DATE / / RECRUITMENT ATTACHE/OR DOCTOR: HISTORY OF ANY SIGNIFICANT PAST ILLNESS INCLUDING: - PSYCHIATRIC AND NEUROLOGICAL DISORDERS (EPILEPSY, DEPRESSION...) - ALLERGY MEDICAL EXAMINATION LABORATORY INVESTIGATION TYPE OF MEDICAL EXAMINATION NEGATIVE\\ POSITIVE\\ TYPE OF LABORATORY NEGATIVE\\ POSITIVE\\ NORMAL ABNORMAL INVESTIGATION NORMAL ABNORMAL VISION R. EYE (URINE) L. EYE - SUGAR EYE - ALBUMIN OTHER R. EYE - BILHARZIASIS L. EYE - OTHER EAR R. EAR (STOOL) - HELMINTHES CHEST X - RAY - SALMONELLA/SHIGELLA PULMONARY TUBERCULOSIS - V.CHOLERA (SYSTEMIC EXAMINATION) - OTHER BLOOD PRESSURE (BLOOD) HEART - HEMOGLOBIN LUNGS - MALARIA FILM ABDOMEN - OTHERS (OTHERS) (SEROLOGY) *HERNIA - HIV TEST *VARICOSE VEINS EXTREMITIES -F.B.S. SKIN - HBSAG/ANTI HCV (VENEREAL DISEASES VDRL TPHA PREGNANCY TEST CONFIRM IF THE APPLICATION HAS ONE OF THE FOLLOWING: NO YES COMMUNICABLE DISEASES MENTAL DISORDER MENTAL RETARDATION PHYSICAL DISORDERS HANDICAP PARALYSIS BLINDNESS HEARING DISORDER SPEECH DISORDER MENTIONED ABOVE IS THE MEDICAL REPORT FOR MR/ MRS/ MISS » WHOIS [ ] FIT [ ] UNFIT FOR THE ABOVE MENTIONED JOB. -TO BE FIT, ALL MEDICAL EXAMINATIONS AND LABORATORY INVESTIGATIONS MUST BE WITHIN NORMAL LIMITS. IN THE EVENT OF AN ABNORMAL/POSITIVE RESULT, A TYPEWRITTEN LETTER SIGNED BY THE PHYSICIAN STATING THE CONDITION AND ANY TREATMENT IMPLEMENTED. THIS LETTER SHOULD ALSO INDICATE WHETHER THIS CONDITION OR TREATMENT WILL HAVE ANY EFFECT ON THE APPLICANT’S WORK. PHYSICIAN NAME: SIGNATURE: LICENSE NUMBER: STAMP: THIS FORM MUST BE ATTESTED BY ONE OF THE TWO FOLLOWING AUTHORITIES: DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH THIS IS TO CERTIFY THAT DR. LICENSE NUMBER: i (2) IS CURRENTLY LICENSED TO PRACTICE MEDICINE. qd) AUTHORIZED SIGNATURE : STAMP OR SEAL OF THE STATE AUTHORITY (COLLEGE OF PHYSICIANS) SUBMIT TO THE CONSULAR SECTION THREE ORIGINALS COPIES OF THIS MEDICAL REPORT AND TWO COPIES OF ALL RESULTS OF THE MEDICAL TESTS. DO NOT SUBMIT X-RAYS AS THOSE MUST BE PRESENTED TO THE HEALTH AUTHORITIES IN SAUDI ARABIA ALONG WITH ONE CLEAR COPY OF THIS REPORT AND ALL TEST RESULTS.'', ''relevance_score'': 0.7089726379534882}, {''title'': ''Medical-report-1-2048'', ''content'': ''a MEDICAL REPORT = (2 8 cigs NAME: NATIONALITY: | SEX: | AGE: MARITAL STATUS: PASSPORT NO: | ISSUE PLACE: | ISSUE DATE: POSITION APPLIED FOR: PHOTO DEAR SIR/ MADAM PLEASE, ARRANGE TO EXAMINE THE ABOVE MENTIONED CANDIDATE AS TO HIS/HER FITNESS FOR THE ABOVE MENTIONED POSITION. DATE / / RECRUITMENT ATTACHE/OR DOCTOR: HISTORY OF ANY SIGNIFICANT PAST ILLNESS INCLUDING: - PSYCHIATRIC AND NEUROLOGICAL DISORDERS (EPILEPSY, DEPRESSION...) - ALLERGY MEDICAL EXAMINATION LABORATORY INVESTIGATION TYPE OF MEDICAL EXAMINATION NEGATIVE\\ POSITIVE\\ TYPE OF LABORATORY NEGATIVE\\ POSITIVE\\ NORMAL ABNORMAL INVESTIGATION NORMAL ABNORMAL VISION R. EYE (URINE) L. EYE - SUGAR EYE - ALBUMIN OTHER R. EYE - BILHARZIASIS L. EYE - OTHER EAR R. EAR (STOOL) - HELMINTHES CHEST X - RAY - SALMONELLA/SHIGELLA PULMONARY TUBERCULOSIS - V.CHOLERA (SYSTEMIC EXAMINATION) - OTHER BLOOD PRESSURE (BLOOD) HEART - HEMOGLOBIN LUNGS - MALARIA FILM ABDOMEN - OTHERS (OTHERS) (SEROLOGY) *HERNIA - HIV TEST *VARICOSE VEINS EXTREMITIES -F.B.S. SKIN - HBSAG/ANTI HCV (VENEREAL DISEASES VDRL TPHA PREGNANCY TEST CONFIRM IF THE APPLICATION HAS ONE OF THE FOLLOWING: NO YES COMMUNICABLE DISEASES MENT