INSERT INTO messages VALUES(86,18,'assistant',unistr('I’d be happy to help summarize a medical report—please share the key details or sections you’d like summarized (e.g., diagnosis, lab results, treatment plan, etc.). For example:\u000a\u000a- Is this a lab report, imaging results, or clinical notes?\u000a- What specific information should I focus on (symptoms, findings, recommendations)?\u000a\u000a**Reminder:** I am an AI assistant for informational support only. Not a substitute for professional medical advice. Always consult a healthcare professional for interpretation of reports or specific concerns.'),'','2026-07-29 08:31:18.033773');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(87,17,'user','what is the attched report about','','2026-07-29 08:31:28.249366');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(88,17,'assistant',unistr('I can''t directly view or analyze attached files (like PDFs, images, or documents). However, if you **describe the key details** from the report—such as:\u000a\u000a- **Type of report** (e.g., lab test, X-ray, doctor’s note, pathology)\u000a- **Key sections/findings** (e.g., "My blood sugar was 120 mg/dL," "The MRI shows a torn ligament")\u000a- **Any medical terms or values** you’d like explained\u000a\u000a—I can summarize or clarify the information for you.\u000a\u000a**Example:**\u000a*"The report is a CBC (complete blood count) with high white blood cells (15,000/µL) and low hemoglobin (9 g/dL). What does this mean?"*\u000a\u000aLet me know how I can help!\u000a\u000a**Disclaimer:** I am an AI assistant for informational support only. Not a substitute for professional medical advice. Always consult a healthcare professional for interpretation.'),'','2026-07-29 08:31:33.491923');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(89,18,'user','summarize the whole report','','2026-07-29 08:33:35.902991');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(90,18,'assistant',unistr('To summarize the report accurately, I’ll need the **content of the report itself** (e.g., key sections like patient history, lab results, imaging findings, diagnosis, or treatment recommendations). Since you haven’t provided details, here’s how I can help:\u000a\u000a1. **Share the report text** (or key excerpts), and I’ll summarize the medical findings concisely.\u000a2. **Specify the type of report** (e.g., blood test, MRI, doctor’s notes) to focus the summary.\u000a\u000a**Example summary structure** (if I had the details):\u000a*"The report indicates [condition/diagnosis], supported by [key findings, e.g., elevated lab values or imaging results]. The recommended next steps include [treatment/referral/follow-up]."*\u000a\u000a**Important:** I am an AI assistant for informational support only. Not a substitute for professional medical advice. Always consult a healthcare professional to interpret reports.'),'','2026-07-29 08:33:41.791606');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(91,19,'user','tell me what is there in this report?','','2026-07-29 08:34:10.297023');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(92,19,'assistant',unistr('I’d be happy to help interpret a medical report, but I’ll need you to share the details of the report (e.g., lab results, imaging findings, or doctor’s notes). Since you haven’t provided specific information, here’s how I can assist:\u000a\u000a1. **If it’s a lab report**: I can explain common terms like CBC (complete blood count), lipid panel, glucose levels, or thyroid function tests.\u000a2. **If it’s an imaging report (X-ray, MRI, CT, ultrasound)**: I can clarify terms like "lesion," "fracture," "inflammation," or "normal findings."\u000a3. **If it’s a doctor’s summary**: I can help explain diagnoses, medications, or next steps mentioned.\u000a\u000a**Please share the key details or findings from the report**, and I’ll provide a clear, concise explanation.\u000a\u000a*Reminder: I am an AI assistant for informational support only. Not a substitute for professional medical advice. Always consult a healthcare professional for personalized interpretation.*'),'','2026-07-29 08:34:15.591330');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(93,20,'user','I have a long beep sound in my ear, for about a year , what is it','','2026-07-29 08:37:53.524706');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(94,20,'assistant',unistr('The long beep or ringing sound you''re experiencing in your ear is most likely **tinnitus**. Tinnitus is the perception of sound when no actual external noise is present. It can manifest as ringing, buzzing, hissing, whistling, or beeping, and can be temporary or chronic.\u000a\u000a### Possible Causes:\u000a1. **Age-related hearing loss** (common in older adults)\u000a2. **Exposure to loud noise** (e.g., concerts, machinery, headphones)\u000a3. **Earwax blockage** (can cause pressure and sound distortion)\u000a4. **Ear or sinus infections**\u000a5. **Medication side effects** (e.g., high doses of aspirin, certain antibiotics, or diuretics)\u000a6. **Temporomandibular joint (TMJ) disorders**\u000a7. **High blood pressure or vascular issues**\u000a8. **Ménière’s disease** (a disorder of the inner ear)\u000a9. **Stress or depression** (can worsen tinnitus)\u000a\u000a### What You Can Do:\u000a- **Consult an ENT (Ear, Nose, and Throat) specialist** to rule out underlying conditions like earwax buildup, infections, or hearing loss.\u000a- **Avoid loud noises** and use ear protection if needed.\u000a- **Manage stress** (tinnitus can worsen with anxiety or fatigue).\u000a- **Limit caffeine, alcohol, and nicotine**, as they can aggravate symptoms.\u000a- **Get a hearing test** if the sound persists, as hearing loss often accompanies tinnitus.\u000a\u000aSince your symptoms have lasted a year, it’s important to seek medical evaluation to determine the cause and explore treatment options (e.g., sound therapy, hearing aids, or counseling).\u000a\u000a*I am an AI assistant for informational support only. Not a substitute for professional medical advice. Always consult a healthcare professional.*'),'[{''title'': ''images-2'', ''content'': ''Patient Information Form Name: Date: Wendi your problem stat?; __escibe Probe Cause of Current Problem: (D caracdent Cl Woskinuy CO Gaduatonset other Did this Problem require Surgery: No 