blems Bowed C1 Heat mebiems 1D Kidney Prabiems Wir then aol we G CanentWoundskinPrebems ©) Galbaddener Og ute Pacemaker 1 ectrclimpant © smoing 1 Tmoucancer sity atch: Headaches C Oisbete 1D Seep Apnea 1D NoSurgeries SugeniesMospeaations ver Complains 1D NoMedicaton Medications Peselt Medations that you ae taking eda) Dove FawsonorMeseaton TT No Keown allergies Allergies latex Ove Ome Todine Ove Ne Bromine Ws Cl no other Do you have anyreigiousicltrlvews that wil affect your treatment?” No Over ‘tional commentieading or Memory Problem) Signature bate'', ''relevance_score'': 0.7376969925666872, ''source'': ''image:images-2.png''}, {''title'': ''WhatsApp Image 2026-07-29 at 12.44.30'', ''content'': ''OG junction, fundus and body of stomach mildly extending into pyloric region with maximum thickness measuring around 26 mm. Associated significant perigastric fat stranding with minimal free fluid noted. Focal suspicious anteromedial outpouching noted involving D3 and D4 part of duodenum with air foci - likely duodenal diverticulum. KIDNEYS: Bilateral kidneys are normal in size. * Renal veins are normal. Bilateral kidneys are showing prompt, synchronous excretion. No evidence of calculus / hydronephrosis. . . « Surface is smooth. e Perinephric spaces are normal. PELVIS o Urinary bladder appears partially distended. co Prostate appears normal in size and attenuation. PERITONEAL CAVITY & OMENTUM Ill-defined omental haziness with nodular enhancement seen involving infrarenal region in anterior aspect. Associated peritoneal thickening noted. Moderate ascites noted. No evidence of appendicitis. ¢ No evidence of adrenal mass lesion. ¢ Bones appear normal. Visualized soft tissues appear normal. . ¢ Abdominal wall normal. IMPRESSION: 1. Significant diffuse circumferential wall thickening involving the distal esophagus, OG junction, fundus, and body of the stomach (up to 26 rr with associated perigastric fat stranding. Findings are highly suspicion malignancy.'', ''relevance_score