INSERT INTO messages VALUES(98,20,'assistant',unistr('I cannot recommend specific medications, brands (like **1mg**), or online pharmacies, as **prescribing treatments for stomach cancer requires a licensed oncologist’s evaluation** based on:\u000a- Cancer stage (early vs. advanced)\u000a- Histopathology (e.g., adenocarcinoma, signet-ring cell)\u000a- Genetic markers (HER2, PD-L1 status)\u000a- Patient’s overall health (age, kidney/liver function)\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **General Treatment Options for Stomach Cancer**\u000a*(For informational purposes only—consult your oncologist for personalized care)*\u000a\u000a#### **1. Early-Stage Cancer (Localized)**\u000a- **Surgery**: Primary treatment (e.g., **gastrectomy**—partial or total stomach removal).\u000a- **Chemotherapy**: Often given **before surgery (neoadjuvant)** to shrink tumors or **after (adjuvant)** to kill remaining cells.\u000a  - Common drugs: **Fluorouracil (5-FU), Capecitabine, Oxaliplatin, Docetaxel**.\u000a- **Targeted Therapy**: If HER2-positive (e.g., **Trastuzumab**).\u000a- **Immunotherapy**: For PD-L1-positive tumors (e.g., **Pembrolizumab**).\u000a\u000a#### **2. Advanced/Metastatic Cancer**\u000a- **Chemotherapy**: First-line regimens like **FOLFOX (5-FU + Oxaliplatin + Leucovorin)** or **FLOT (5-FU + Oxaliplatin + Docetaxel)**.\u000a- **Targeted Therapy**:\u000a  - **Trastuzumab** (HER2-positive).\u000a  - **Ramucirumab** (VEGFR2 inhibitor, used with Paclitaxel).\u000a- **Immunotherapy**: **Pembrolizumab** or **Nivolumab** (for MSI-H/dMMR or PD-L1-positive tumors).\u000a- **Palliative Care**: To manage symptoms (e.g., **pain relief, nutritional support**).\u000a\u000a#### **3. Supportive Medications**\u000a- **Antacids/PPIs** (e.g., **Omeprazole, Pantoprazole**) for acid reflux.\u000a- **Anti-nausea drugs** (e.g., **Ondansetron, Aprepitant**) for chemotherapy side effects.\u000a- **Pain management** (e.g., **NSAIDs, Opioids** if severe).\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **Critical Notes**\u000a1. **Never self-medicate**—stomach cancer drugs have severe side effects (e.g., neuropathy, heart toxicity) and require monitoring.\u000a2. **Genetic testing** (e.g., HER2, MSI, PD-L1) guides therapy. Ask your doctor about **precision medicine**.\u000a3. **Clinical trials** may offer access to newer drugs (e.g., **Zolbetuximab** for CLDN18.2-positive tumors).\u000a4. **Nutrition is key**—consult a dietitian to manage weight loss and malnutrition (common in stomach cancer).\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **What You Can Do Now**\u000a- **Ask your oncologist**:\u000a  - Is my cancer **HER2-positive** or **PD-L1-positive**? (Affects immunotherapy eligibility.)\u000a  - Are there **clinical trials** for my stage?\u000a  - What are the **side effects** of recommended drugs?\u000a- **Lifestyle**: Eat small, frequent meals; avoid spicy/acidic foods; stay hydrated.\u000a\u000a*I am an AI assistant for informational support only. Not a substitute for professional medical advice. Always consult your oncologist for diagnosis and treatment.*'),'[{''title'': ''WhatsApp Image 2026-07-29 at 12.44.29'', ''content'': ''ors’ Dive! Dads Doct Aeti Speceeloy (Laat of rRICHY Mr.Xavier ™ jent Name 2)Gender ent UID ferring From 82Y 7)RO0729517 mR Hospital (tr) ws MS..MCH, ferring Doctor: OF Mathes Test Dysphagia for evaluation 1.Groumferend growt Clinical Data on lesser curv re 2.Mutipple nodu 3.Duodenum - 0 Specimen <=> _s ss yt LKQ) ah involving 3507 of two LSpecimen consss & 2. Specimen consis f NLA ys 0aad 260131 56 sample 10 ‘ 901371/2026 Histopath No Registered On : 21/01/2026 7:22 PM Collected on + 21/01/2026 7:23 PM Reported On 22/01/2026 7:02 PI HISTOPATHOLOGICAL EXAMINATION incisors, extending to proximal stomach, Je on greater curvature D2 - Multiple nodule. — Sxtatees'', ''relevance_score'': 0.7554932822952074, ''source'': ''image:WhatsApp Image 2026-07-29 at 12.44.29.jpeg''}, {''title'': ''WhatsApp Image 2026-07-29 at 12.44.30'', ''content'': ''OG junction, fundus and bod