INSERT INTO messages VALUES(104,22,'assistant',unistr('Based on Emily Johnson’s cardiology report, here’s a summary of the key details:\u000a\u000a**Medical History:**\u000a- Emily has a **3-year history of hypertension**, which she manages with medication.\u000a- **No known drug allergies**.\u000a- **Family history of coronary artery disease** (her father had it).\u000a- She is a **non-smoker** and generally maintains an **active lifestyle**.\u000a\u000a**Presenting Complaints:**\u000a- **Intermittent chest pain**, primarily during physical exertion.\u000a- **Occasional palpitations** (irregular or rapid heartbeats) over the last two months.\u000a- **Shortness of breath** during jogging, which was previously well-tolerated.\u000a\u000a**Diagnostic Tests Conducted:**\u000aThe report mentions that diagnostic tests were performed, but the specific results are not fully visible in the provided image. Typically, for symptoms like hers, tests may include:\u000a- **Electrocardiogram (ECG/EKG)** to check heart rhythm.\u000a- **Echocardiogram** to assess heart structure and function.\u000a- **Stress test** to evaluate heart performance under exertion.\u000a- **Blood tests** (e.g., lipid profile, cardiac enzymes).\u000a- **Holter monitor** (if palpitations are frequent) to track heart activity over time.\u000a\u000a**Possible Concerns:**\u000aHer symptoms (chest pain on exertion, shortness of breath, palpitations) and family history suggest a need to rule out **coronary artery disease, arrhythmias, or worsening hypertension**. The management plan would likely focus on further evaluation, lifestyle adjustments, and possibly medication adjustments.\u000a\u000a**Recommendation:**\u000aFor a precise diagnosis and treatment plan, Emily should follow up with her cardiologist, who will interpret the test results and provide personalized guidance.\u000a\u000a*I am an AI assistant for informational support only. Not a substitute for professional medical advice. Always consult a healt