ack, stroke) - Neuropathy (nerve damage) - Nephropathy (kidney damage) - Retinopathy (eye damage, potential blindness) - Foot damage (risk of amputation) - Skin conditions - Hearing impairment - Alzheimer''s disease", ''relevance_score'': 0.757202977717265, ''source'': ''diabetes_overview.md''}, {''title'': ''WhatsApp Image 2026-07-29 at 12.44.29'', ''content'': ''ors’ Dive! Dads Doct Aeti Speceeloy (Laat of rRICHY Mr.Xavier ™ jent Name 2)Gender ent UID ferring From 82Y 7)RO0729517 mR Hospital (tr) ws MS..MCH, ferring Doctor: OF Mathes Test Dysphagia for evaluation 1.Groumferend growt Clinical Data on lesser curv re 2.Mutipple nodu 3.Duodenum - 0 Specimen <=> _s ss yt LKQ) ah involving 3507 of two LSpecimen consss & 2. Specimen consis f NLA ys 0aad 260131 56 sample 10 ‘ 901371/2026 Histopath No Registered On : 21/01/2026 7:22 PM Collected on + 21/01/2026 7:23 PM Reported On 22/01/2026 7:02 PI HISTOPATHOLOGICAL EXAMINATION incisors, extending to proximal stomach, Je on greater curvature D2 - Multiple nodule. — Sxtatees'', ''relevance_score'': 0.7567899896242615, ''source'': ''image:WhatsApp Image 2026-07-29 at 12.44.29.jpeg''}]','2026-07-29 09:05:56.981922');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(107,21,'user','Psychiatric and Anti-Anxiety Tablets','','2026-07-29 09:06:48.197299');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(108,21,'assistant',unistr('For **psychiatric and anti-anxiety medications**, doctors may prescribe different classes of drugs depending on the **specific mental health condition** (e.g., anxiety, depression, insomnia, PTSD, or agitation in dementia). Below is a **general overview** of common medications used, but **only a psychiatrist or healthcare provider should prescribe them** after a proper evaluation.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **1. Anti-Anxiety Medications (Anxiolytics)**\u000a#### **A. Benzodiazepines (Fast-Acting, Short-Term Use)**\u000a- **Used for:** Acute anxiety, panic attacks, insomnia, agitation.\u000a- **Examples:**\u000a  - **Alprazolam (Xanax)** – Short-acting, for panic attacks.\u000a  - **Lorazepam (Ativan)** – Intermediate-acting, for anxiety or sleep.\u000a  - **Diazepam (Valium)** – Long-acting, for generalized anxiety or muscle spasms.\u000a  - **Clonazepam (Klonopin)** – For chronic anxiety or seizures.\u000a- **⚠️ Risks:**\u000a  - **Addiction & dependence** (especially with long-term use).\u000a  - **Drowsiness, confusion, falls** (high risk in elderly).\u000a  - **Withdrawal symptoms** if stopped abruptly.\u000a\u000a#### **B. Non-Benzodiazepine Anxiolytics (Safer for Long-Term Use)**\u000a- **Buspirone (Buspar)** – For generalized anxiety disorder (GAD), non-addictive.\u000a- **Hydroxyzine (Atarax, Vistaril)** – Antihistamine with mild anti-anxiety effects (sedating).\u000a- **Beta-Blockers (e.g., Propranolol)** – For **physical symptoms of anxiety** (e.g., rapid heartbeat, tremors).\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **2. Antidepressants (Also Used for Anxiety & Chronic Stress)**\u000a#### **A. SSRIs (Selective Serotonin Reuptake Inhibitors) – First-Line for Anxiety/Depression**\u000a- **Used for:** Generalized anxiety, depression, OCD, PTSD.\u000a- **Examples:**\u000a  - **Escitalopram (Lexapro, Cipralex)**\u000a  - **Sertraline (Zoloft, Lustral)**\u000a  - **Fluoxetine (Prozac)**\u000a  - **Paroxetine (Paxil, Seroxat)**\u000a- **⚠️ Side Effects:**\u000a  - Nausea, insomnia, sexual dysfunction, weight gain.\u000a  - **Takes 4-6 weeks to work.**\u000a  - **Risk of increased suicidal thoughts in young adults (rare in elderly).**\u000a\u000a#### **B. SNRIs (Serotonin-Norepinephrine Reuptake Inhibitors)**\u000a- **Used for:** Anxiety, depression, chronic pain (e.g., neuropathy).\u000a- **Examples:**\u000a  - **Venlafaxine (Effexor)**\u000a  - **Duloxetine (Cymbalta)**\u000a- **⚠️ Side Effects:** Similar to SSRIs, plus **increased blood pressure.**\u000a\u000a#### **C. Atypical Antidepressants**\u000a- **Mirtazapine (Remeron)** – Helps with **sleep + appetite** (good for elderly with depression & weight loss).\u000a- **Bupropion (Wellbutrin)** – For **depression + ADHD**, less sexual side effects (but can cause insomnia).\u000a- **Trazodone** – Mostly used for **insomnia** (low-dose) or depression (high-dose).\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **3. Mood Stabilizers (For Bipolar Disorder or Severe Mood Swings)**\u000a- **Lithium** – Classic mood stabilizer (requires **blood level monitoring**).\u000a- **Valproate (Depakote)** – For bipolar disorder or agitation.\u000a- **Lamotrigine (Lamictal)** – For bipolar depression (low risk of weight gain).\u000a- **Quetiapine (Seroquel)** – Atypical antipsychotic, also used for **anxiety + insomnia**.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **4. Antipsychotics (For Severe Anxiety, Agitation, or Psychosis)**\u000a- **Used for:** Severe anxiety, PTSD, agitation in dementia, schizophrenia.\u000a- **Examples:**\u000a  - **Quetiapine (Seroquel)** – Low-dose for anxiety/sleep.\u000a  - **Olanzapine (Zyprexa)** – For agitation or bipolar disorder.\u000a  - **Risperidone (Risperdal)** – For aggression in dementia (use cautiously).\u000a  - **Aripiprazole (Abilify)** – For depression augmentation or bipolar disorder.\u000a- **⚠️ Risks:**\u000a  - **Weight gain, diabetes, movement disorders (tardive dyskinesia).**\u000a  - **Increased stroke risk in elderly with dementia.**\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **5.'),'[{''title'': ''images-2'', ''content'': ''Patient Information Form Name: Date: Wendi your problem stat?; __escibe Probe Cause of Current Problem: (D caracdent Cl Woskinuy CO Gaduatonset other Did this Problem require Surgery: No Cl Yes 0 YesDateot surgery ast Medical History Oo youhaveaisry fhe fosoning problems? 2 Breathing Pblems D Seok 2 Depression Pregnant 1D BonajeintPeblems Bowed C1 Heat mebiems 1D Kidney Prabiems Wir then aol we G CanentWoundskinPrebems ©) Galbaddener Og ute Pacemaker 1 ectrclimpant © smoing 1 Tmoucancer sity atch: Headaches C Oisbete 1D Seep Apnea 1D NoSurgeries SugeniesMospeaations ver Complains 1D NoMedicaton Medications Peselt Medations that you ae taking eda) Dove FawsonorMeseaton TT No Keown allergies Allergies latex Ove Ome Todine Ove Ne Bromine Ws Cl no other Do you have anyreigiousicltrlvews that wil affect your treatment?” No Over ‘tional commentieading or Memory Problem) Signature bate'', ''relevance_score'': 0.6853848011230371, ''source'': ''image:images-2.png''}, {''title'': ''images-2'', ''content'': ''Patient Information Form Name: Date: Wendi your problem stat?; __escibe Probe Cause of Current Problem: (D caracdent Cl Woskinuy CO Gaduatonset other Did this Problem require Surgery: No Cl Yes 0 YesDateot surgery ast Medical History Oo youhaveaisry fhe fosoning problems? 2 Breathing Pblems D Seok 2 Depression Pregnant 1D BonajeintPeblems Bowed C1 Heat mebiems 1D Kidney Prabiems Wir then aol we G CanentWoundskinPrebems ©) Galbaddener Og ute Pacemaker 1 ectrclimpant © smoing 1 Tmoucancer sity atch: Headaches C Oisbete 1D Seep Apnea 1D NoSurgeries SugeniesMospeaations ver Complains 1D NoMedicaton Medications Peselt Medations that you ae taking eda) Dove FawsonorMeseaton TT No Keown allergies Allergies latex Ove Ome Todine Ove Ne Bromine Ws Cl no other Do you have anyreigiousicltrlvews that wil affect your treatment?” No Over ‘tional commentieading or Memory Problem) Signature bate