INSERT INTO messages VALUES(109,21,'user','Psychiatric and Anti-Anxiety Tablets','','2026-07-29 09:52:48.287754');
INSERT INTO messages VALUES(110,21,'assistant',unistr('Here’s a **concise, medically accurate** overview of **psychiatric and anti-anxiety medications**, categorized by their primary use. **Always consult a psychiatrist or doctor before starting, adjusting, or stopping any medication.**\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **1. Anti-Anxiety Medications (Anxiolytics)**\u000a#### **A. Benzodiazepines (Fast-Acting, Short-Term Use)**\u000a- **Use:** Acute anxiety, panic attacks, insomnia, muscle spasms, alcohol withdrawal.\u000a- **Examples:**\u000a  - **Short-acting:** Alprazolam (Xanax), Lorazepam (Ativan)\u000a  - **Long-acting:** Diazepam (Valium), Clonazepam (Klonopin)\u000a- **⚠️ Risks:**\u000a  - **Dependence & withdrawal** (must taper slowly).\u000a  - **Drowsiness, confusion, falls** (especially in elderly).\u000a  - **Avoid alcohol** (increases sedation).\u000a\u000a#### **B. Non-Benzodiazepine Alternatives (Safer for Long-Term Use)**\u000a- **Buspirone (Buspar)** – For **generalized anxiety disorder (GAD)**, non-addictive.\u000a- **Hydroxyzine (Atarax, Vistaril)** – Antihistamine with mild anti-anxiety effects (sedating).\u000a- **Beta-Blockers (Propranolol, Atenolol)** – For **physical symptoms of anxiety** (e.g., rapid heartbeat, tremors).\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **2. Antidepressants (Also Used for Anxiety & Chronic Stress)**\u000a#### **A. SSRIs (First-Line for Anxiety & Depression)**\u000a- **Use:** GAD, panic disorder, OCD, PTSD, depression.\u000a- **Examples:**\u000a  - Escitalopram (Lexapro, Cipralex)\u000a  - Sertraline (Zoloft, Lustral)\u000a  - Fluoxetine (Prozac)\u000a  - Paroxetine (Paxil, Seroxat)\u000a- **⚠️ Side Effects:**\u000a  - Nausea, insomnia, sexual dysfunction, weight gain.\u000a  - **Takes 4–6 weeks to work.**\u000a  - **Risk of increased suicidal thoughts in young adults (rare in elderly).**\u000a\u000a#### **B. SNRIs (For Anxiety + Chronic Pain)**\u000a- **Use:** GAD, depression, neuropathic pain.\u000a- **Examples:**\u000a  - Venlafaxine (Effexor)\u000a  - Duloxetine (Cymbalta)\u000a- **⚠️ Side Effects:** Similar to SSRIs, plus **increased blood pressure.**\u000a\u000a#### **C. Atypical Antidepressants**\u000a- **Mirtazapine (Remeron)** – Helps with **sleep + appetite** (good for elderly with depression).\u000a- **Bupropion (Wellbutrin)** – For **depression + ADHD**, less sexual side effects (but can cause insomnia).\u000a- **Trazodone** – Mostly used for **insomnia** (low-dose) or depression (high-dose).\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **3. Mood Stabilizers (For Bipolar Disorder or Severe Mood Swings)**\u000a- **Lithium** – Classic mood stabilizer (**requires blood level monitoring**).\u000a- **Valproate (Depakote)** – For bipolar disorder or agitation.\u000a- **Lamotrigine (Lamictal)** – For bipolar depression (low risk of weight gain).\u000a- **Quetiapine (Seroquel)** – Atypical antipsychotic, also used for **anxiety + insomnia**.\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **4. Antipsychotics (For Severe Anxiety, Agitation, or Psychosis)**\u000a- **Use:** Severe anxiety, PTSD, agitation in dementia, schizophrenia.\u000a- **Examples:**\u000a  - **Quetiapine (Seroquel)** – Low-dose for anxiety/sleep.\u000a  - **Olanzapine (Zyprexa)** – For agitation or bipolar disorder.\u000a  - **Risperidone (Risperdal)** – For aggression in dementia (use cautiously).\u000a  - **Aripiprazole (Abilify)** – For depression augmentation or bipolar disorder.\u000a- **⚠️ Risks:**\u000a  - **Weight gain, diabetes, movement disorders (tardive dyskinesia).**\u000a  - **Increased stroke risk in elderly with dementia.**\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **5. Sleep Aids (For Insomnia Related to Anxiety/Depression)**\u000a- **Zolpidem (Ambien)** – Short-term sleep aid (risk of dependence).\u000a- **Eszopiclone (Lunesta)** – Longer-acting sleep aid.\u000a- **Doxepin (Silenor)** – Low-dose tricyclic antidepressant for sleep.\u000a- **Melatonin** – Natural sleep regulator (mild effect).\u000a\u000a---\u000a\u000a### **⚠️ Critical Warnings:**\u000a1'),'[{''title'': ''images-2'', ''content'': ''Patient Information Form Name: Date: Wendi your problem stat?; __escibe Probe Cause of Current Problem: (D caracdent Cl Woskinuy CO Gaduatonset other Did this Problem require Surgery: No Cl Yes 0 YesDateot surgery ast Medical History Oo youhaveaisry fhe fosoning problems? 2 Breathing Pblems D Seok 2 Depression Pregnant 1D BonajeintPeblems Bowed C1 Heat mebiems 1D Kidney Prabiems Wir then aol we G CanentWoundskinPrebems ©) Galbaddener Og ute Pacemaker 1 ectrclimpant © smoing 1 Tmoucancer sity atch: Headaches C Oisbete 1D Seep Apnea 1D NoSurgeries SugeniesMospeaations ver Complains 1D NoMedicaton Medications Peselt Medations that you ae taking eda) Dove FawsonorMeseaton TT No Keown allergies Allergies latex Ove Ome Todine Ove Ne Bromine Ws Cl no other Do you have anyreigiousicltrlvews that wil affect your treatment?” No Over ‘tional commentieading or Memory Problem) Signature bate'', ''relevance_score'': 0.6853848011230371, ''source'': ''image:images-2.png''}, {''title'': ''images-2'', ''content'': ''Patient Information Form Name: Date: Wendi your problem stat?; __escibe Probe Cause of Current Problem: (D caracdent Cl Woskinuy CO Gaduatonset other Did this Problem require Surgery: No Cl Yes 0 YesDateot surgery ast Medical History Oo youhaveaisry fhe fosoning problems? 2 Breathing Pblems D Seok 2 Depression Pregnant 1D BonajeintPeblems Bowed C1 Heat mebiems 1D Kidney Prabiems Wir then aol we G CanentWoundskinPrebems ©) Galbaddener Og ute Pacemaker 1 ectrclimpant © smoing 1 Tmoucancer sity atch: Headaches C Oisbete 1D Seep Apnea 1D NoSurgeries SugeniesMospeaations ver Complains 1D NoMedicaton Medications Peselt Medations that you ae taking eda) Dove FawsonorMeseaton TT No Keown allergies Allergies latex Ove Ome Todine Ove Ne Bromine Ws Cl no other Do you have anyreigiousicltrlvews that wil affect your treatment?” No Over ‘tional commentieading or Memory Problem) Signature bate'', ''relevance_score'': 0.6853848011230371,